# corpus: deliberate-decline -- stage0 initializes a writable global reference from readonly
# string-literal storage; stage1 correctly rejects the readonly-to-writable capability upgrade.
# Rule R: a global declared with a writable reference type must be initialised from a
# writable reference; a string literal's bytes are readonly.
global g: mutable u8& = "abc"

def main() -> i32:
    return 0
